Root Cause                                                                      

 • Faulty component: frontend-proxy-7b7cd5fb4-jsr6n (container frontend‑proxy)  
 • Misconfiguration: Memory limit set to 65 MiB (Limits: memory: 65Mi). The     
   proxy process exceeds this limit, causing the container to be OOMKilled      
   repeatedly (restart count = 4) and entering a back‑off state.                
 • Why it breaks the app: The frontend‑proxy routes traffic to all other        
   services. When it is OOM‑killed and not ready, the UI cannot reach downstream
   services, resulting in a complete outage for the shop front‑end.             

Evidence                                                                        

 1 kubectl describe pod – shows State: Terminated – Reason: OOMKilled, Exit     
   Code: 137, Restart Count: 4, Limits: memory: 65Mi.                           
 2 Pod events include Warning BackOff for the container.                        
 3 Prometheus alert KubePodNotReady firing for this pod.                        
 4 All other pods are running and ready, confirming the issue is isolated to the
   frontend‑proxy.                                                              

Remediation                                                                     

 1 Increase memory resources for the frontend-proxy container (e.g., requests:  
   128Mi, limits: 256Mi).                                                       
 2 Apply the change via the Helm chart (or Deployment manifest) and roll out the
   update:                                                                      
                                                                                
    helm upgrade astronomy-shop ./chart \                                       
      --set frontendProxy.resources.limits.memory=256Mi \                       
      --set frontendProxy.resources.requests.memory=128Mi \                     
      -n astronomy-shop                                                         
                                                                                
 3 Verify the pod becomes Ready and the alert clears:                           
                                                                                
    kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready pod -l                                   
    app.kubernetes.io/name=frontend-proxy -n astronomy-shop --timeout=2m        
                                                                                
 4 Monitor the pod’s memory usage (kubectl top pod frontend-proxy-…) to ensure  
   the new limits are sufficient.                                               

Impact                                                                          

 • Affected: frontend-proxy-7b7cd5fb4-jsr6n (OOMKilled, not ready).             
 • Checked, healthy: All other 26 pods in the astronomy-shop namespace.         
 • Changed for another reason: None observed.                                   

After increasing the memory limits and confirming the pod stabilises, the       
OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop should resume normal operation.               

